WEBVTT

00:00:16.030 --> 00:00:19.430
London Bridge is broken down,

00:00:19.430 --> 00:00:22.810
broken down, broken down...

00:00:22.810 --> 00:00:25.990
London Bridge is broken down,

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:29.620
my fair lady...

00:00:32.230 --> 00:00:34.400
I'll be seeing you soon,

00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:36.470
Sister.

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:51.980
London Steam

00:01:02.090 --> 00:01:03.530
Captain Leonhardt.

00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:06.730
Preparations to storm 
the mansion are complete.

00:01:06.730 --> 00:01:07.660
Good work.

00:01:08.230 --> 00:01:09.980
It's so quiet.

00:01:09.980 --> 00:01:13.080
Is this really where the target is?

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:16.270
Do not lower your guard 
under any circumstances.

00:01:16.270 --> 00:01:20.360
That is our credo as knights,
 as swords in service to the Queen.

00:01:20.690 --> 00:01:21.470
Sir!

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:23.100
Besides...

00:01:24.440 --> 00:01:26.510
We're up against a monster.

00:01:28.190 --> 00:01:29.580
<i>I hear voices.</i>

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:37.220
<i>Why have they awakened me?</i>

00:01:38.050 --> 00:01:41.440
<i>I wished to remain in my 
warm sleep forever...</i>

00:01:42.210 --> 00:01:46.820
<i>All I wanted was to spend my life 
in warm, comfortable sleep.</i>

00:01:49.660 --> 00:01:50.840
This must be it.

00:02:18.810 --> 00:02:21.130
That's... the monster?

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:29.860
And here I wondered what kind 
of terrible monster it'd be.

00:02:29.860 --> 00:02:31.420
She's just a girl.

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:32.410
Fool!

00:02:33.140 --> 00:02:33.910
Don't...

00:02:42.070 --> 00:02:43.460
M-Monster!

00:02:43.460 --> 00:02:44.180
Don't move!

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:45.880
Move and we'll shoot!

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:48.150
Don't lose your heads!

00:02:49.240 --> 00:02:51.310
You would point a firearm at a lady?

00:02:51.310 --> 00:02:54.180
And you call yourselves soldiers 
of the proud British Army?

00:02:54.180 --> 00:02:56.040
But, Captain...

00:02:56.040 --> 00:02:57.190
Capture her.

00:02:57.470 --> 00:03:00.090
But do so respectfully.

00:03:10.990 --> 00:03:12.780
Will you shut up already?!

00:03:13.250 --> 00:03:15.200
Aw, what's your problem?

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:18.020
You need to be more aware 
of how serious this is.

00:03:18.020 --> 00:03:20.990
We're about to steal the 
treasure of a lifetime!

00:03:21.320 --> 00:03:23.970
How long do we have to wait 
here telling ourselves that?

00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:27.050
Are you sure those guys 
are gonna pass by here?

00:03:27.780 --> 00:03:30.540
Okay, listen. Being a thief means—

00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:33.970
Having the patience to take all precautions 
and wait for the right moment?

00:03:34.240 --> 00:03:35.810
Heard that before.

00:03:35.810 --> 00:03:37.770
Here ya go. All done.

00:03:38.910 --> 00:03:41.690
Are you sure this will work?

00:03:41.690 --> 00:03:45.520
Hey, I'm the world's number one genius 
engineer. You have my guarantee.

00:03:45.520 --> 00:03:48.200
I can't think of anything I'd trust 
less than your guarantee...

00:03:50.620 --> 00:03:51.450
Is it them?

00:03:53.670 --> 00:03:54.320
No...

00:03:54.710 --> 00:03:56.220
That's the British Army.

00:03:56.220 --> 00:03:57.050
What?!

00:03:57.330 --> 00:03:59.140
That's not what our intel said!

00:03:59.140 --> 00:04:02.060
Do you really wanna pick 
a fight with Queen Victoria?

00:04:02.060 --> 00:04:04.560
Shouldn't we rethink our plan?

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:06.760
No. We proceed as planned.

00:04:06.760 --> 00:04:09.570
You'll wait at the rendezvous 
point, as discussed.

00:04:09.570 --> 00:04:10.560
Seriously?

00:04:10.560 --> 00:04:13.850
Where's that "patience to take all precautions
 and wait for the right moment"?

00:04:14.160 --> 00:04:16.330
There's more to that saying.

00:04:17.710 --> 00:04:22.640
"And at times, you must also be daring. 
Otherwise, you can't be a thief."

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:31.730
Troops, halt!

00:04:32.190 --> 00:04:33.810
On your guard!

00:04:42.350 --> 00:04:44.940
A job well done, gentlemen.

00:04:45.240 --> 00:04:48.780
The personal guard forces of the proud 
British Royal Family, committing a kidnapping?

00:04:48.780 --> 00:04:52.010
Her Majesty the Queen must 
be quite proud, indeed.

00:04:52.890 --> 00:04:54.690
You insult us?!

00:04:54.690 --> 00:04:57.010
Just who the hell are you?!

00:04:57.540 --> 00:05:00.120
My name is Arsène Lupin.

00:05:00.120 --> 00:05:02.670
Really, I'm undeserving of such alarm.

00:05:02.670 --> 00:05:06.750
I'm merely your run-of-the-mill 
dashing gentleman thief!

00:05:07.520 --> 00:05:09.900
Gentleman thief?

00:05:10.340 --> 00:05:13.520
My prize tonight is the captured princess.

00:05:13.800 --> 00:05:18.410
Behold, as I rescue her with style from 
the hands of you poorly-trained dogs.

00:05:18.420 --> 00:05:19.840
What was that?!

00:05:20.350 --> 00:05:21.510
Shoot him!

00:05:43.840 --> 00:05:45.580
Calm down, all of you!

00:05:45.580 --> 00:05:48.650
Don't scatter! Maintain tight formation!

00:05:49.670 --> 00:05:51.770
I can't give commands in this...

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:55.710
This is...

00:05:59.800 --> 00:06:01.630
Th-This smoke...

00:06:02.380 --> 00:06:05.670
is no... mere... smoke...

00:06:14.620 --> 00:06:17.280
Damn that Impey. This is way too much.

00:06:20.100 --> 00:06:21.150
You—

00:06:22.420 --> 00:06:24.720
Come, princess. Your hand.

00:06:27.100 --> 00:06:30.690
Oh, yeah... You have some scary 
poison or something, right?

00:06:30.990 --> 00:06:34.230
But those gloves are meant 
to contain it, aren't they?

00:06:34.810 --> 00:06:36.340
How did you...

00:06:41.080 --> 00:06:43.910
Don't worry. Just trust me.

00:06:47.110 --> 00:06:49.290
Allow me to introduce myself once more.

00:06:49.590 --> 00:06:51.790
My name is Arsène Lupin.

00:06:52.180 --> 00:06:55.720
For certain reasons, I have 
come to steal your heart.

00:06:57.260 --> 00:06:59.000
My... heart?

00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:01.810
Yes, precisely that. Your heart.

00:07:02.450 --> 00:07:05.310
What do... you... mean...

00:07:05.620 --> 00:07:09.330
Ah, I guess the drug from 
the smokescreen is kicking in.

00:07:12.270 --> 00:07:14.450
Goodnight, princess.

00:07:25.100 --> 00:07:26.350
<i>Cardia,</i>

00:07:26.910 --> 00:07:29.810
<i>you must never leave this mansion.</i>

00:07:30.580 --> 00:07:31.680
<i>Because...</i>

00:07:32.360 --> 00:07:34.190
<i>you are a monster.</i>

00:07:40.170 --> 00:07:42.840
Man, there goes the steam engine again...

00:07:42.840 --> 00:07:47.550
Jeez, Impey... You sure this hunk of 
junk will get us to the mansion?

00:07:49.720 --> 00:07:52.780
What's with the big doe eyes?

00:07:53.560 --> 00:07:56.460
Are you surprised to see how handsome I am?

00:07:56.460 --> 00:07:57.550
No.

00:07:58.160 --> 00:08:00.290
No sense of humor...

00:08:01.170 --> 00:08:03.370
Oh, Cardia! You're awake?

00:08:03.660 --> 00:08:06.660
Hey! Nice to meet ya, cutie!

00:08:06.660 --> 00:08:10.130
I'm the ultra gorgeous genius 
engineer and great inventor,

00:08:10.130 --> 00:08:12.560
as well as the man who'll 
stand on the moon one day,

00:08:12.560 --> 00:08:14.190
Impey Barbicane!

00:08:14.710 --> 00:08:17.510
Call me Impey. Glad to know ya.

00:08:17.760 --> 00:08:19.710
Nice to... meet you...

00:08:20.080 --> 00:08:22.760
Um, how do you know my name?

00:08:22.760 --> 00:08:26.250
Well, we've been trying 
to find you forever.

00:08:26.250 --> 00:08:27.760
Of course we know your name.

00:08:28.030 --> 00:08:32.480
Still, I didn't think the treasure you 
told me about would be this cute!

00:08:32.480 --> 00:08:33.440
Impey.

00:08:33.440 --> 00:08:36.460
Just shut up and fix this 
hunk of junk already.

00:08:36.460 --> 00:08:37.780
Oh, sure, sure.

00:08:39.560 --> 00:08:44.040
Okay, my little engine baby, 
cheer up for me, okay?

00:08:46.060 --> 00:08:47.300
There! All set!

00:08:49.280 --> 00:08:52.160
Sorry about that. She's so stubborn.

00:08:52.160 --> 00:08:57.290
Of course, at your request, I'd be glad to 
perform love maintenance for you, too.

00:08:58.040 --> 00:09:00.380
I'll tune you up tonight.

00:09:03.210 --> 00:09:04.530
Er, huh?

00:09:04.870 --> 00:09:07.600
Just hurry up and start the car, Impey.

00:09:07.600 --> 00:09:10.070
We'll never get back at this rate.

00:09:10.310 --> 00:09:11.560
Yeah, yeah.

00:09:25.390 --> 00:09:27.860
Oh, you've never seen it before, have you?

00:09:28.240 --> 00:09:30.830
That's industrial London.

00:09:31.410 --> 00:09:35.140
Home of our beloved Queen Victoria,

00:09:35.430 --> 00:09:39.560
and the political and economical center of 
not only England, but the whole world.

00:09:43.620 --> 00:09:46.840
So you've never been to a big city before?

00:09:47.310 --> 00:09:49.610
Then you and I should take 
a little time to...

00:09:50.730 --> 00:09:53.350
No way! Those things are 
floating around now?

00:09:53.590 --> 00:09:55.740
He's sure got it rough.

00:09:55.740 --> 00:09:59.240
If Saint hadn't taken him in, 
he'd probably be behind bars.

00:09:59.240 --> 00:10:00.780
You said it.

00:10:00.780 --> 00:10:02.250
A terrorist?

00:10:02.680 --> 00:10:05.340
Yep. He's a <i>super bad</i> guy.

00:10:05.340 --> 00:10:07.740
You can decide whether he's 
bad or not soon enough.

00:10:08.190 --> 00:10:10.120
We'll be there soon.

00:10:10.120 --> 00:10:11.060
"There"?

00:10:11.060 --> 00:10:13.450
Yep, at our stronghold.

00:10:17.610 --> 00:10:19.760
Cardia, this way!

00:10:20.730 --> 00:10:22.070
We're back!

00:10:23.190 --> 00:10:24.510
We just got in.

00:10:25.630 --> 00:10:27.260
Welcome back, you two.

00:10:27.870 --> 00:10:29.160
Good work.

00:10:31.130 --> 00:10:33.360
Here, Fran. A souvenir for you.

00:10:33.360 --> 00:10:36.320
Wow... That's a problem.

00:10:36.320 --> 00:10:38.920
Well, it won't last.

00:10:38.920 --> 00:10:42.550
The British government is busy
 fighting wars against other nations.

00:10:43.010 --> 00:10:46.650
By the way, your sleep drug 
worked like a charm.

00:10:46.870 --> 00:10:48.910
Oh, was it useful for you?

00:10:48.910 --> 00:10:53.090
Cardia, this is Fran. He's one of us.

00:10:53.090 --> 00:10:55.920
I'm Victor Frankenstein. Nice to meet you.

00:10:56.250 --> 00:10:57.910
Nice to meet you...

00:10:57.910 --> 00:11:00.670
There's one other guy, Saint, but...

00:11:00.670 --> 00:11:04.300
Saint is, well... sort of like our patron.

00:11:04.570 --> 00:11:07.620
He lets us use this mansion.

00:11:07.970 --> 00:11:10.280
I'm sure he'll show up sooner or later.

00:11:10.680 --> 00:11:12.640
Lupin, is she...

00:11:12.640 --> 00:11:14.690
Yep, no doubt about it.

00:11:15.830 --> 00:11:18.320
She's Isaac Beckford's daughter.

00:11:19.360 --> 00:11:21.830
You know... my father?

00:11:24.610 --> 00:11:26.480
Isaac Beckford.

00:11:26.480 --> 00:11:29.200
There's no one in England 
who doesn't know his name.

00:11:29.910 --> 00:11:30.950
That's right.

00:11:31.230 --> 00:11:35.390
London wouldn't be nearly
 as prosperous without him.

00:11:36.860 --> 00:11:39.390
He's a one-of-a-kind genius.

00:11:40.000 --> 00:11:42.200
Completely on his own,

00:11:42.200 --> 00:11:45.810
Isaac created things that should be 
impossible to make with today's science.

00:11:46.570 --> 00:11:49.220
The perpetual motion machine, 
the Horologium...

00:11:49.610 --> 00:11:51.840
Horologium?

00:11:52.930 --> 00:11:56.240
It's also known as the 
eternally-beating heart,

00:11:56.600 --> 00:12:00.760
capable of infinitely creating
 massive amounts of energy.

00:12:01.240 --> 00:12:05.240
Isaac embedded it in his 
own daughter's body.

00:12:07.170 --> 00:12:09.740
The British Army tried to kidnap you

00:12:09.740 --> 00:12:12.170
because they wanted that Horologium.

00:12:12.740 --> 00:12:14.150
The British Army?

00:12:14.150 --> 00:12:15.300
That's right.

00:12:15.300 --> 00:12:19.570
They were using the Queen's 
personal guard as their pawns.

00:12:19.570 --> 00:12:20.590
You're kidding...

00:12:21.050 --> 00:12:22.140
I...

00:12:22.750 --> 00:12:24.010
never knew

00:12:25.450 --> 00:12:27.670
what this thing was,

00:12:28.550 --> 00:12:33.500
or why such a terrible poison 
resides in my body.

00:12:35.640 --> 00:12:38.510
I don't know anything.

00:12:39.200 --> 00:12:40.770
Cardia...

00:12:45.580 --> 00:12:47.360
This is your room.

00:12:47.830 --> 00:12:52.550
You must be tired, right? 
So call it a night and... wait...

00:12:52.550 --> 00:12:54.610
How do you usually sleep?

00:12:54.610 --> 00:12:58.040
My bed at the mansion, 
much like my clothes,

00:12:58.040 --> 00:12:59.900
was made so the poison wouldn't dissolve it.

00:12:59.900 --> 00:13:03.590
This bed... would dissolve, wouldn't it?

00:13:03.830 --> 00:13:06.160
My hair won't dissolve anything,

00:13:06.160 --> 00:13:08.250
so if I sleep on my back, 
it should be fine.

00:13:08.430 --> 00:13:09.520
Okay, then.

00:13:10.010 --> 00:13:13.360
I guess I'll ask Fran if he can 
do anything about the rest...

00:13:14.140 --> 00:13:17.400
Until then, well... just do your best.

00:13:18.620 --> 00:13:19.560
See ya.

00:13:20.640 --> 00:13:21.610
Lupin...

00:13:23.270 --> 00:13:26.290
When can I return to the mansion?

00:13:27.660 --> 00:13:30.930
Didn't I tell you?
 I came to steal your heart—

00:13:34.360 --> 00:13:35.490
Whoa, hey!

00:13:36.160 --> 00:13:39.480
Wh-What are you doing, you idiot?!

00:13:39.480 --> 00:13:42.370
By "heart," do you mean the Horologium?

00:13:43.020 --> 00:13:46.380
Why does everyone want these jewels?

00:13:47.660 --> 00:13:49.690
I don't know anything

00:13:50.230 --> 00:13:53.880
about my father, or even about myself.

00:13:54.970 --> 00:13:58.720
I have no memories prior to two years ago.

00:13:59.570 --> 00:14:04.390
Please tell me. Why did my 
father put this thing in me?

00:14:04.650 --> 00:14:07.970
A-All right! Just cover yourself back up!

00:14:08.360 --> 00:14:09.420
Why?

00:14:09.650 --> 00:14:11.980
Because that's how a lady's 
supposed to behave!

00:14:12.370 --> 00:14:13.760
Okay.

00:14:13.760 --> 00:14:18.160
Sheesh... Do you know what might've 
happened if I weren't a gentleman?

00:14:18.770 --> 00:14:23.170
All I know about Isaac is 
what I told you earlier.

00:14:23.370 --> 00:14:27.810
So I don't know why he put 
that thing in your chest,

00:14:28.200 --> 00:14:31.980
but I do know why everyone wants it.

00:14:33.260 --> 00:14:37.180
The guys who tried to kidnap you 
last night were the British Army,

00:14:37.670 --> 00:14:40.030
but the guys manipulating 
them from the shadows

00:14:40.030 --> 00:14:42.930
are most likely Twilight.

00:14:43.380 --> 00:14:44.640
Twilight?

00:14:45.070 --> 00:14:49.220
They want to use the Horologium 
to do something horrible.

00:14:50.140 --> 00:14:53.670
A large-scale terrorist plot that 
would overthrow all of London.

00:14:54.070 --> 00:14:57.990
And Isaac's intentions have 
something to do with that.

00:14:59.110 --> 00:15:02.820
You mean my father is planning 
a terrorist attack?

00:15:03.160 --> 00:15:06.880
The reason I captured you was to stop them.

00:15:07.330 --> 00:15:10.730
We can't let Twilight have the Horologium.

00:15:11.820 --> 00:15:15.110
Sorry, but I can't let you go home.

00:15:15.620 --> 00:15:17.030
But I...

00:15:17.630 --> 00:15:19.250
can't stay here.

00:15:20.350 --> 00:15:21.840
I can't.

00:15:24.760 --> 00:15:27.450
You must be tired. For now...

00:15:28.170 --> 00:15:29.350
get some rest.

00:15:33.150 --> 00:15:34.960
I will see this through.

00:15:35.570 --> 00:15:38.500
If that can be my atonement...

00:15:40.840 --> 00:15:43.390
I'm right, aren't I, Master?

00:15:44.620 --> 00:15:46.740
You are a monster.

00:15:46.740 --> 00:15:49.180
You bring misfortune to others.

00:15:49.180 --> 00:15:52.930
That is why you must live 
your life in isolation.

00:15:53.620 --> 00:15:54.640
Father...

00:16:01.670 --> 00:16:03.890
G-Good evening.

00:16:12.210 --> 00:16:14.410
Do you live in this mansion?

00:16:20.700 --> 00:16:22.750
Your leg...

00:16:32.620 --> 00:16:34.000
She's gone?!

00:16:34.300 --> 00:16:36.660
Maybe she just got lost in the mansion?

00:16:36.660 --> 00:16:39.090
I looked for her. She's not here!

00:16:39.460 --> 00:16:41.630
You're the one who last 
saw her, right, Lupin?

00:16:41.630 --> 00:16:43.230
How was she acting then?

00:16:43.230 --> 00:16:44.980
How was she acting? Well...

00:16:45.620 --> 00:16:48.380
She was confused... I guess.

00:16:48.380 --> 00:16:50.890
No kidding! Of course she's confused!

00:16:50.890 --> 00:16:54.400
You didn't say, "You can never escape, 
ga-ha-ha," or anything, did you?!

00:16:56.270 --> 00:16:58.660
I didn't make it sound that crude.

00:16:58.660 --> 00:17:00.610
But you said something like it?!

00:17:02.030 --> 00:17:04.280
Unbelievable! And you call 
yourself a gentleman?

00:17:05.750 --> 00:17:07.360
She must have been scared,

00:17:07.790 --> 00:17:10.290
suddenly being kidnapped 
and confined like that...

00:17:10.290 --> 00:17:13.670
We didn't confine her! 
She's free to come and go—

00:17:15.440 --> 00:17:17.080
Maybe she's trying...

00:17:18.410 --> 00:17:20.170
to go back home?

00:17:20.430 --> 00:17:22.760
Wait, that would be really, really bad!

00:17:22.760 --> 00:17:27.180
Cardia's got Twilight, the British Army 
and half the world after her!

00:17:27.370 --> 00:17:29.810
We should split up and look for her.

00:17:43.080 --> 00:17:44.200
Thank goodness.

00:17:44.450 --> 00:17:47.590
It's cold out here. Let's go back inside.

00:17:52.280 --> 00:17:53.340
Don't...

00:17:56.370 --> 00:17:56.960
No!

00:18:03.280 --> 00:18:04.530
Cardia!

00:18:06.960 --> 00:18:08.850
Don't scare me like that.

00:18:09.170 --> 00:18:10.070
I couldn't...

00:18:12.470 --> 00:18:15.990
I couldn't help. It died.

00:18:15.990 --> 00:18:17.480
Because of me.

00:18:18.800 --> 00:18:20.980
My father was right.

00:18:21.430 --> 00:18:23.310
I am a monster.

00:18:23.770 --> 00:18:26.020
I bring misfortune to others.

00:18:26.850 --> 00:18:29.440
That is why I must live 
my life in isolation.

00:18:37.640 --> 00:18:38.420
No.

00:18:40.870 --> 00:18:44.220
There's no one in this world 
who has to live in isolation.

00:18:45.180 --> 00:18:47.940
You need to value yourself more.

00:18:51.430 --> 00:18:53.340
My angel!

00:18:53.340 --> 00:18:54.500
I'm so glad we found you!

00:18:54.500 --> 00:18:56.690
Cardia, we were so worried!

00:18:57.210 --> 00:18:59.410
Stay here, Cardia.

00:18:59.690 --> 00:19:02.690
Sisi seems to have taken 
a liking to you, too.

00:19:04.700 --> 00:19:07.850
All right! Let's all throw 
her a welcome party!

00:19:07.850 --> 00:19:11.020
Right now? Shouldn't we go to bed?

00:19:11.020 --> 00:19:12.960
We can sleep tomorrow!

00:19:11.950 --> 00:19:13.440
Noisy, aren't they?

00:19:12.960 --> 00:19:15.060
All right! Let's have a blast!

00:19:13.440 --> 00:19:16.090
They're not bad to have as buddies, though.

00:19:17.420 --> 00:19:18.770
Buddies?

00:19:20.160 --> 00:19:21.250
Lupin...

00:19:22.370 --> 00:19:27.380
I still don't know if I should stay here.

00:19:28.330 --> 00:19:29.390
But...

00:19:32.050 --> 00:19:36.000
This place seems warm.

00:19:36.870 --> 00:19:38.610
Then you should stay.

00:19:38.880 --> 00:19:41.220
Do what you want to do.

00:19:41.220 --> 00:19:43.820
What I want to do?

00:19:43.820 --> 00:19:48.060
Don't you want to know 
more about this world?

00:19:48.060 --> 00:19:49.320
About your father?

00:19:49.630 --> 00:19:52.340
And don't you want to know about yourself?

00:19:53.410 --> 00:19:57.190
You don't have to wait. 
We can go looking for it.

00:19:57.920 --> 00:20:00.920
I'm Arsène Lupin, the gentleman thief.

00:20:01.260 --> 00:20:03.590
Whatever I want, I steal.

00:20:04.260 --> 00:20:07.920
If you stay with us, you'll 
find your answers eventually.

00:20:13.640 --> 00:20:15.880
Glad you're here, Cardia.

00:20:35.740 --> 00:20:38.450
Don't freeze up on me, miss.

00:20:42.500 --> 00:20:47.220
Let's see... I told you I was going 
to steal that precious heart,

00:20:47.500 --> 00:20:52.220
so in return, I'll grant one wish for you.

00:20:52.620 --> 00:20:53.680
A wish?

00:20:55.470 --> 00:20:56.910
Yes, indeed.

00:20:57.220 --> 00:21:04.130
This humble thief swears to grant 
your wish, and that's the truth.

00:21:04.990 --> 00:21:05.860
I have none.

00:21:07.780 --> 00:21:09.300
I can't think of a wish.

00:21:09.610 --> 00:21:14.350
I've never even thought 
about what I'd wish for.

00:21:15.920 --> 00:21:17.290
Is that right?

00:21:17.800 --> 00:21:19.820
Well, no need to rush.

00:21:20.850 --> 00:21:22.600
Let's go, Cardia.

00:21:23.850 --> 00:21:27.540
<i>My heart responds to his words.</i>

00:21:27.930 --> 00:21:32.460
<i>Something that I thought was tightly 
sealed deep within my chest</i>

00:21:32.460 --> 00:21:34.380
<i>seems to be rattling as it stirs.</i>

00:21:36.720 --> 00:21:40.200
<i>I want to know many things.</i>

00:21:41.210 --> 00:21:43.290
<i>Where is my father?</i>

00:21:43.930 --> 00:21:47.450
<i>And just what am I?</i>
